    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d289">

                <pb facs="0398" n="278" sameAs="frus:frus1905/pg278"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Cuban Minister to the Secretary of
                    State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of Cuba</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1905-02-10"><hi rendition="#italic">February 10,
                        1905</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 194.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: In compliance with the wishes of
                    your Department expressed in the memorandum of January 26, replying to mine of
                    the 19th idem., I have the honor to inclose copies of testimony in the case of
                    the injury suffered by the Cuban citizen, Felipe Maza é Ibarra, at the hands of
                    United States soldiers.<anchor n="a" xml:id="d289-f1"/></p>
                <p>Relying upon the high spirit of justice of your excellency, I venture to ask that
                    as an act of grace toward the unfortunate citizen, Maza é Ibarra, an allowance
                    be made to relieve his miserable condition.</p>
                <p>I take, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gonzales de
                    Quesada.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
